From d0b3096ff0f6f6f491833858f126a80f18b81151 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dmitry Stogov <dmitry@zend.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Sep 2022 11:38:31 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] Reset FG(user_stream_current_filename) at the end of request

A bailout inside a user stream wrapper's stream_open or dir_opendir left
the recursion guard pointing into the finished request, so a later request
of the same process could read freed memory and fail with "infinite
recursion prevented" when it opened the same URL.

Origin: upstream, https://github.com/php/php-src/commit/d0b3096ff0f6f6f491833858f126a80f18b81151
---
diff --git a/main/streams/streams.c b/main/streams/streams.c
index fbcc1ca4..365bc023 100644
--- a/main/streams/streams.c
+++ b/main/streams/streams.c
@@ -1633,6 +1633,7 @@ static void stream_resource_persistent_dtor(zend_rsrc_list_entry *rsrc TSRMLS_DC
 
 void php_shutdown_stream_hashes(TSRMLS_D)
 {
+	FG(user_stream_current_filename) = NULL;
 	if (FG(stream_wrappers)) {
 		zend_hash_destroy(FG(stream_wrappers));
 		efree(FG(stream_wrappers));
